# Completion priorities

When asked to continue or complete this project, prioritize work based on the existing `COMPLETION_GUIDE.md` and current repo state.

## Known completed / polished areas (verify in repo before skipping)

- Home hero: Three.js globe (`HeroGlobePlexus`) and Earth asset; loader polish
- Why Choose Ensemble, CTABand, ServiceTiers, About hero, Contact: theme token alignment (partial site-wide pass)
- PageTransition uses `window.locomotiveScroll` (verify behavior on navigation)
- Some nav/footer/content/design iteration

## Known remaining priorities (may include)

- Confirm font file placement and paths under `public/fonts/`
- Wire contact form and newsletter to real backend or service
- Add privacy, terms, and disclaimer routes or external links
- Replace placeholder footer/contact details with final production data
- Extend theme tokens to Services grid, FAQ, Case Studies, carousels where raw grays remain
- Finalize trust logos, case study content, about content, and insights content (hero uses globe; optional background video via `content.js`)
- Optional: lazy-load `HeroGlobePlexus` for smaller main bundle
- Add insight detail route if needed
- Final SEO, favicon, metadata, and production build testing

## How to work on completion

- Check whether a task is already finished before changing it
- Do not duplicate previously completed work
- Prefer finishing incomplete production-critical areas before making cosmetic-only changes
- Prioritize functionality, route completeness, content readiness, and deployment readiness after major UI polish is in place

Read `COMPLETION_GUIDE.md` and `documents/` logs before assuming what is left to do.
